<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="69461" href="schedule/2019/spring/ECE/598/69461.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="ECE" href="schedule/2019/spring/ECE.xml">Electrical and Computer Engineering</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2019/spring/ECE/598.xml">Special Topics in ECE</course></parents><sectionNumber>JZ </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Radio-Freq IC &amp; System Dsgn</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Radio-Frequency IC Design This course will cover basic principles of modern wireless transceiver design using integrated circuit technology at radio frequency (RF) (~100MHz to 6GHz) for wireless communication applications, such as LTE and WiFi. Building upon the analog IC skills learned from ECE 483 - Analog IC Design, this new course teaches analysis and design of integrated circuits and systems that operate at much higher frequencies and for wireless communications in specific. Prerequisites: ECE 483 and one of three courses (ECE 453, ECE 447, or ECE 457) required.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2022</roomNumber><buildingName>Electrical &amp; Computer Eng Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Zhou" firstName="J">Zhou, J</instructor></instructors></meeting><meeting id="1"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>11:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>3013</roomNumber><buildingName>Electrical &amp; Computer Eng Bldg</buildingName><instructors><i